  "decision": "Guard-free page-aligned probes supersede the earlier c1 boundary: 129,024 total tokens (126 Ki, 504 pages) is the highest observed working Qwen3.8-27B pure-INT8 c1 row on the RX 7900 XTX, completing one exact natural request at 23.962624 GiB peak with 0.021751 GiB sampled headroom and clean ownership. The next page, 129,280 tokens, stalls raw startup warmup beyond 600 seconds; 130,048 tokens returns HIP OOM. The strongest repeated natural c1 evidence remains four exact 114,688-token requests at 23.322876 GiB peak with 0.661499 GiB headroom. At c2, every tested row through 6,144 tokens/request completed, while 8,192 failed both requests with HIP OOM and 8,448 failed startup because direct no-mirror packed INT8 is unsupported. Physical c4 completed 1,536/request for 16/16 multi-turn requests, and no c4 execution failure was tested. Shape-aware offered-c8 rows execute as queue groups capped at physical c4; offered c8 completed every tested row through 2,048/request, although that highest raw row predates shape capture, and no c8 execution failure was observed. The short c>1 route retains a BF16 mirror and is not an efficient INT8 capacity path.",
